[% META
   title = "Daily log Start Day and End Day fix"
   description = "Start Day was posting twice, so OK showed 'already one for the day'. End Day could report closed while another open row for the same day remained."
   roles = "admin,developer"
   TemplateType = "Documentation"
   category = "planning"
   page_version = "0.01"
   last_updated = "2026-11-20"
   site_specific = "false"
   project_id = "138"
   project_code = "PLANNING"
%]
[% PageVersion = 'Documentation/DailyLogStartEndFix.tt,v 0.01 2026/11/20 hermes-agent Exp shanta ' %]
[% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %][% PageVersion %][% END %]

<div class="container">
[% INCLUDE 'admin/documentation/_doc_header.tt'
    page_title = 'Daily log Start Day and End Day fix'
    last_updated = '2026-11-20'
    doc_project_id = 138
    doc_project_code = 'PLANNING'
%]

<div class="doc-info" id="now">
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Now.</strong> Start Day posts once. End Day closes every open daily-log row for that user and date, then re-reads the row. If the status did not become closed, the page gets an error instead of "closed".</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Blocked by.</strong> Nothing in code. The change is in the planning worktree only. Port 3001 will not show it until this branch is merged. JavaScript needs a hard refresh. The Perl change is picked up by the running <code>-r</code> server on port 4005 when <code>Planning.pm</code> is saved.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Next.</strong> Hard-refresh <a class="doc-link" href="/planning/daily">/planning/daily</a> on the planning server, click Start Day once, then End Day once. The day should stay closed after reload.</p>
</div>

